  "name": "COXSACHIE ANTIBODY - IgM",
  "code": "2715",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p>The <strong data-start=\"58\" data-end=\"89\">Coxsackie Antibody IgM test</strong> detects <strong data-start=\"98\" data-end=\"116\">IgM antibodies</strong> against the <strong data-start=\"129\" data-end=\"148\">Coxsackie virus</strong>, a member of the <strong data-start=\"166\" data-end=\"181\">Enterovirus</strong> group. It is primarily used to identify <strong data-start=\"222\" data-end=\"253\">recent or current infection</strong> with Coxsackievirus.</p>\n<p data-start=\"1282\" data-end=\"1311\"><strong data-start=\"1286\" data-end=\"1311\">Clinical Significance</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"1313\" data-end=\"1737\">\n<li data-start=\"1313\" data-end=\"1409\">\n<p data-start=\"1315\" data-end=\"1409\"><strong data-start=\"1315\" data-end=\"1331\">Positive IgM</strong> supports recent infection, especially when consistent with clinical symptoms.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1410\" data-end=\"1643\">\n<p data-start=\"1412\" data-end=\"1463\">May be elevated in <strong data-start=\"1431\" data-end=\"1451\">Coxsackie A or B</strong> infections:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"1466\" data-end=\"1643\">\n<li data-start=\"1466\" data-end=\"1545\">\n<p data-start=\"1468\" data-end=\"1545\"><strong data-start=\"1468\" data-end=\"1483\">Coxsackie A</strong>: Often linked to hand, foot, and mouth disease or herpangina.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1548\" data-end=\"1643\">\n<p data-start=\"1550\" data-end=\"1643\"><strong data-start=\"1550\" data-end=\"1565\">Coxsackie B</strong>: Associated with myocarditis, pericarditis, and other systemic complications.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1644\" data-end=\"1737\">\n<p data-start=\"1646\" data-end=\"1737\">May also help evaluate <strong data-start=\"1669\" data-end=\"1690\">unexplained fever</strong>, <strong data-start=\"1692\" data-end=\"1708\">viral rashes</strong>, or <strong data-start=\"1713\" data-end=\"1736\">neurologic symptoms</strong>.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Test Result</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Interpretation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Positive IgM</strong></td>\n<td>Indicates a <strong>recent or active Coxsackievirus infection</strong>. IgM typically appears within a few days of symptom onset and may persist for weeks.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Negative IgM</strong></td>\n<td>No evidence of recent infection. Either no exposure, the test was done too early (before IgM formed), or the infection is in the past.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Equivocal/Borderline</strong></td>\n<td>Inconclusive; may need repeat testing or correlation with clinical findings and IgG titers.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
